// REFACTOR:grounded (#320, plan585): explicit age publication replaces legacy age authoring and lowering; unrelated contracts are retained.
# DME101.030 — Ultrasonic Osteogenesis Stimulator
library "Ultrasonic Osteogenesis Stimulator Coverage".

/*
Mixed migration regression fixture, not a current authoring model.
The Patient-age declaration has migrated. Remaining existence-based local answers,
device merging and Scalar interfaces exercise retained legacy machinery. In particular,
the presence of a coded Observation cannot stand in for its Boolean answer value.
Historical $apply results do not make these remaining declarations current guidance.
Use the Bleph acceptance fixture and supported selected-publication examples for
current authoring; preserve this fixture only for its owning regression assertions.
*/

// ============ Supplied determinations — value concept + boolean interface (both-rep convention) ============

// Legacy covered-device ValueSet. For this
// round-trip fixture we control the terminology with made-up codes we own, so it is a small explicit
// set; this reference remains a synthetic terminology fixture.
terminology "Covered Devices":
- valueset is `http://example.org/hcsc/dme101-030/ValueSet/covered-devices`.

// Age publication accepts Patient.birthDate or its own Boolean answer. A same-day assertion wins
// over today's calculation; otherwise current calculation supersedes older assertions. Missing
// input remains unknown. Numeric age entry is a separate, unimplemented assertion point.
concept "Adult Eighteen Or Older":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `adult-18-or-older`.
- shape reduction is most recent.
- source representation:
  - type is Patient.
  - value projection is age today at least 18 years.

// The requested device — the VALUE concept (North Star §3). A `CodeableConcept` datum, both-rep:
// the REMOTE arm DEFAULTS the code from the supplied `ServiceRequest.code`; the LOCAL arm SETS or
// OVERRIDES it, and `most recent this` recency-merges them (newest wins). `coded from "Covered
// Devices"` scopes it to the covered set, so a non-covered request does not populate it (closed-world
// → absent). EMIT-CATCH-UP (#257 general posrep + the `code is`+reduction+`source representation`
// 3-way #189 slice) — validates clean today; emit must catch up. Do not delete or downgrade.
concept "Covered Device":
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- code is `covered-device`.
- definition is most recent this.
- source representation:
  - type is ServiceRequest.
  - coded from "Covered Devices".

// The coverage determination — the BOOLEAN INTERFACE concept (North Star §3). It USES the value
// concept: `defined as exists ("Covered Device")` is true when a covered device is present (from
// either arm), false otherwise. Directly assertable via its own local `code is`.
concept "Covered Device Requested":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `covered-device-requested`.
- defined as exists ("Covered Device").

// ============ Clinical determinations (local-code Observations — asserted inferences) ============

concept "Fracture Of Skull Or Vertebrae":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `skull-or-vertebrae-fracture`.
- definition is exists this.

concept "Tumor-Related Fracture":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `tumor-related-fracture`.
- definition is exists this.

concept "Documented Fracture Nonunion":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `documented-fracture-nonunion`.
- definition is exists this.

// ============ Decision ============

decision "Ultrasonic Osteogenesis Stimulator Coverage":
first:
- when not "Covered Device Requested" then recommend activity "not-certify.Unmet".
- when "Fracture Of Skull Or Vertebrae" then recommend activity "not-certify.Deny".
- when "Tumor-Related Fracture" then recommend activity "not-certify.Deny".
- when not "Adult Eighteen Or Older" then recommend activity "not-certify.Deny".
- when "Documented Fracture Nonunion" then recommend activity "certify.Approve".
- otherwise then recommend activity "not-certify.Deny".

// ============ Activities (shareable PA determinations) ============

activity "certify.Approve":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Prior authorization request approved.`.

activity "not-certify.Deny":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Prior authorization request denied.`.

activity "not-certify.Unmet":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Coverage criteria not met: the requested device is not a covered ultrasonic osteogenesis stimulator.`.
